@@ -27,9 +27,16 @@ One execution of a Job.
 A Run has a stable id and one terminal outcome:
 
 - succeeded;
-- failed.
+- failed;
+- cancelled.
 
-A Run may contain one or more Attempts.
+A Run may contain zero or more Attempts.
+
+A running Run can be cancelled before its first Attempt or between Attempts.
+Cancellation is terminal: it accepts no further Attempts and emits no Alert.
+Cancelling an already cancelled Run succeeds without changing it; succeeded and
+failed Runs retain their outcomes and cannot be cancelled. Cancelled Runs count
+as a Job's most recent terminal result on the Dashboard.
 
